\b \cf0 Late 1985
\b0 :\
Samaritan arrives in the twentieth century.\

\b January 28, 1986
\b0 :\
The debut of Samaritan, saving the space shuttle Challenger. Apperentely, this was the event he was supposed to avert from happening.\

\b May 4, 1989
\b0 \
Jack-In-The-Box returns after an absence of some five and a half years.\

\b 1991
\b0 :\

\i Crackerjack
\i0  debuts.\

\b August 7, 1995
\b0 :\

\i Jack-In-The-Box
\i0  captures 
\i Brass Monkey
\i0 \

\b August 8, 1995
\b0 :\
An average {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://kbac.orcon.net.nz/workday.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \ul \ulc2 workday}} for Samaritan, the most important being the battle between him and the 
\i Living Nightmare
\i0 .\

\b August 9, 1995
\b0 :\

\i Astro City Rocket
\i0  editor Eliot Mills tells his story of how the Honor Guard defeated Shirak the Devourer in 1959 to a rookie reporter.\

\b September 7, 1995
\b0 :\
N-forcer saves senate. (newspaper article in 5:10.1.)\

\b December 11, 1995
\b0 :\
Cleopatra II fights Gnomnicron\

\b December 12, 1995
\b0 :\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ql\qnatural
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}The identity of Crackerjack is revealed.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ql\qnatural
\ls4\ilvl0
\i \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Bridwell
\i0 , an alien spy gives the signal for the 
\i Enelsian
\i0  invasion of Earth.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ql\qnatural

\b \cf0 June 17, 1997
\b0 :\
The Astrobank is robbed by the 
\i Junkman
\i0 , who leaves no clues behind for the heroes to suspect him.\

\b July-August, 1997
\b0 :\
The Enelsian invasion plan is put in high gear, moving into the open when it's revealed that Astro City's Mayor is an alien..\

\b August 03, 1997
\b0 :\
After heated battles with superheroes around the world the Enelsian invasion force is defeated.\

\b November 6, 1997
\b0 :\
The Junkman is captured by Jack-In-The-Box, while attempting to rob the Astrobank for the second time.\

\b 2001
\b0 :\
Brian Kinney, formely Altar Boy returns as the new Confessor.\

\b The 35th century
\b0 :\
The man who would be Samaritan is born, at a time when the Earth is dying.\
After two years of preparation he's sent back in time to the twentieth century, to change the future.\

\b The 35th century, new version
\b0 :\
Samaritan visits the 35th century to discover it's now an utopia, but it has cost him his family, whom now don't exist.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\ql\qnatural
\cf0 This timeline covers only the events for which I have been able to find an (approximate) date. Not all events mentioned in the series have known dates.\
